--
N5008 [class.derived.general]/2: "A class-or-decltype shall denote a
(possibly cv-qualified) class type that is not an incompletely defined
class"; X is incompletely defined in its own base-specifier-list.  The
front end crashes (SIGSEGV, unbounded recursion) instead of reporting the
error.  The same for a class template instance (test_class_template.desc)
and an instance of a partial specialization
(test_partial_specialization.desc).  Pre-existing (bin53).  g++ 13
("invalid use of incomplete type", "recursive type undefined") and
clang++ 18 ("circular inheritance") reject these programs.
